# Build products, and the scratch a play-test round writes.
#
# `.context/` is where every play-test tool writes: probe directories, transcripts,
# the round's derived arguments, and the saved games a tester cuts mid-session. A
# round tells each of its agents to write there and nowhere else, which is only a
# safe instruction if this line exists — without it the first round an author dispatches
# arrives at `git status` as a few hundred untracked files.
.context/
/.build
/dist
.DS_Store

# `.playtest/` is committed, not ignored. `.playtest/<Game>/routes/` holds the deep
# starts a round ships, and a fresh checkout needs them: a route nobody commits is a
# deep start the next clone does not have. Play-test *scratch* belongs under
# `.context/playtest/`, so anything under `.playtest/` that is not a route or a round
# record is a bug worth noticing rather than hiding.
